HST Office: the collapse ladder refills the room a fold leaves, and makes room for the block beside it.

- When the ladder is used up and groups fold into the chevron popup, the groups that stay are laid
  out again with the same ladder for the room that is left, so they do not stay shrunk beside an
  empty gap. The folded set only grows as the window narrows.
- With the ladder on, the merged group box asks its parent for its smallest width (every group at
  its smallest state, nothing folded), so the block beside it in the tab (Home's Tools group) folds
  only when the groups cannot make room for it by shrinking; it no longer folds at 1920 px.
  Switched off (HSTRibbon CollapseLadder), the box asks for its full width as before.

- vcl/source/control/PriorityMergedHBox.cxx, vcl/inc/PriorityMergedHBox.hxx.

